Source: pg-disorder
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/viralpraxis/pg_disorder

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-disorder
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-disorder
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Perturb unordered SELECT results to expose test failures
 pg_disorder is a test-only module that reverses or shuffles rows from eligible
 SELECT statements without ORDER BY. Load it with session_preload_libraries;
 it is not intended for production use.
